1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,146
NASA's Curiosity rover
drove over a rock on Mars.

2
00:00:04,286 --> 00:00:06,589
It cracked open, and this was inside.

3
00:00:07,109 --> 00:00:08,247
Yellow crystals.

4
00:00:08,387 --> 00:00:11,337
Pure sulfur, the first ever found on Mars.

5
00:00:11,857 --> 00:00:13,962
An instrument on the arm confirmed it:

6
00:00:14,102 --> 00:00:15,450
sulfur, on its own.

7
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:20,130
On Earth, pure sulfur forms
near volcanoes and hot springs.

8
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:22,278
There's no evidence of either here.

9
00:00:22,798 --> 00:00:25,358
The mission's project
scientist said it plainly:

10
00:00:25,498 --> 00:00:26,582
it shouldn't be there.

11
00:00:27,102 --> 00:00:30,363
A new study dates it to about
three billion years ago.

12
00:00:30,503 --> 00:00:32,359
How it formed is still debated.

